-- title:
--   Uniform finite Fourier correction for all selected CFZ families
-- statement:
--   Let $k\ge3$ and let $w$ be at least the W-tricked complex CFZ exceptional bound. For every $\varepsilon>0$, eventually in $N$ the product of the normalized small-prime correction and zeta-system factor is within $\varepsilon$ of $1$, uniformly over every selected CFZ exponent pattern and all coordinates in its paired Fourier box of radius $\sqrt{\log\operatorname{sieveLevel}(k,N)}$.
